====================================================================================================
S3. Predicted b-cutoff -- SCANNING the one uncertain input, both error channels
====================================================================================================
  The uncertain input is what fraction of the LCDM non-thermal budget is PECULIAR VELOCITY
  (amplified) as opposed to HUBBLE BROADENING (not amplified -- MI leaves the background
  untouched). Rather than assume it, scan it. Setup at the PEAK of the measured sequence,
  z = 2.8, where b0 = 22.67 +0.55/-0.6 km/s:
  thermal floor b_th = 12.8-18.2 km/s for T = 1-2e4 K
  so the LCDM non-thermal budget at the cutoff is b_nt = sqrt(b_cut^2 - b_th^2) = 18.7 km/s at T = 1e4 K, falling to 13.6 km/s at T = 2e4 K
  using the CONSERVATIVE amplification sqrt(1/h) at z = 2.8, delta = 3: 2.37 canonical, 2.48 alt footing
    f_pec    T (K)    b_th   b_pec   b_hub   b_pred  sig_stat   sig_cal  b_pred alt  sig_stat   sig_cal
