  SCAN RANGE, both footings: statistical 3.3-39 sigma, calibration 0.5-6 sigma
  [OK] EVERY point in the scan, on BOTH footings, predicts a cutoff above the measured 22.67 km/s -- by 3.3-39 sigma on Hiss's statistical bar and 0.5-6 sigma even against the 3.36 km/s calibration systematic, so the result does not depend on the uncertain peculiar/Hubble split
  THRESHOLD (statistical channel): the peculiar-velocity fraction of the LCDM non-thermal
    budget must be below f_pec < 1.57e-02 to stay within 1 sigma of the measurement.
  THRESHOLD (calibration channel): the peculiar-velocity fraction of the LCDM non-thermal
    budget must be below f_pec < 1.02e-01 to stay within 1 sigma of the measurement.
  [OK] survival requires f_pec < 1.6e-02 (statistical) / 1.0e-01 (calibration), i.e. peculiar velocities contributing essentially NOTHING to forest line widths -- which no LCDM hydro simulation supports

