====================================================================================================
S5. DIRECT PRIOR ART -- Aguirre, Schaye & Quataert 2001 -- and the x-CONVENTION FORK
====================================================================================================
  Aguirre, Schaye & Quataert 2001, ApJ 561, 550 (DOI 10.1086/323376; astro-ph/0105184v2),
  'Problems for MOND in Clusters and the Ly-alpha Forest?', applied MOND to forest gas 25
  years before this script. It is genuine prior art on this exact test and must be cited.
  Their Eq. 7 gives the MOND Jeans length L_J ~= 11 kpc (N_HI/1e14)^(-1/5) Gamma_12^(-1/5)
  T_4^0.65, GAS ONLY (MOND posits no dark component), and their Eq. 8 the absorber's internal
  Newtonian acceleration a_N ~= 4e-13 cm/s^2 = 4.00e-15 m/s^2 at N_HI = 1e14, T_4 = 1.
  THREE THINGS THE CORPUS MUST NOT GET WRONG ABOUT THIS PAPER:
   (i) Their verbatim 'The internal acceleration is then ~= a0/170' is the MOND-MODIFIED
       acceleration a = sqrt(a_N a0) = 6.93e-13 m/s^2, NOT a_N/a0. On THEIR
       a0 = 1.2e-10 m/s^2 the Newtonian ratio is a_N/a0 = 1/30000, and the exact
       identity is a_N/a0 = (a/a0)^2 = 1/170^2. The figure '1/23400' appears NOWHERE in the
       paper; it is only what their fixed a_N gives against the framework's canonical a0.
   (ii) Their Omega_gas = 0.008-0.009 vs 0.045 is the ISOLATED case only, they call it
       'still plausible', their external-field value is 0.005-0.03 with the upper end in
       'comfortable agreement', and their stated conclusion is that MOND yields '(for any
       assumed external field) a reasonable density of intergalactic gas'. Relaying it as a
       MOND/forest kill would manufacture a deficit the source does not assert.
   (iii) Their forest verdict is deliberately SOFT and EFE-degenerate -- the title ends in
       '?', the conclusion says '(perhaps) intergalactic gas clouds', and their footnote 7
       concedes the SEP violation 'severely limits the possibility of testing the MOND
       formula over many decades of acceleration'. The kill they DO assert is CLUSTERS.
  NOTE FOR THE FRAMEWORK SPECIFICALLY: their Eq. 1 is the bare deep limit a = sqrt(a_N a0),
  which the framework's own nu(y) = sqrt(1+1/y) reproduces EXACTLY, so their forest
  calculation is interpolation-function-independent and carries over with a0 as the only
  change. But their EFE is the Bekenstein-Milgrom modified-GRAVITY result of Milgrom 1986,
  so it is NOT prior art on a modified-INERTIA external-field prediction.

  THE FORK. a_N for forest gas is CONVENTION-OWNED, not physical. Rebuilding a_N from their
  own relation a_N = (c_s^2/L)^2/a0 across their own sizes and mass components spans:
  convention                          a_N (m/s^2)    x canon  A canon      x alt    A alt  sig_stat   sig_cal
  Aguirre iso MOND, gas, 11 kpc          4.00e-15   4.27e-05      8.7   3.54e-05      9.2      126s       21s
  Aguirre EFE a0/g0=170, 21.1 kpc        2.10e-15   2.24e-05     10.3   1.86e-05     10.8      153s       25s
  Aguirre EFE a0/g0=25, 40 kpc           7.60e-15   8.12e-05      7.4   6.73e-05      7.8      102s       17s
  gas only at CDM size 110 kpc           1.10e-14   1.18e-04      6.8   9.73e-05      7.1       90s       15s
  gas+DM at 300 kpc (obs 'size')         2.50e-14   2.67e-04      5.5   2.21e-04      5.8       68s       11s
  CDM/Newtonian gas+DM, 110 kpc          6.90e-14   7.37e-04      4.3   6.11e-04      4.5       47s        8s
