  amplification 5x, and the z = 2.8 exclusion 3-25 sigma on the
  calibration channel. Both a0 footings are inside every row and they differ by only
  1.21x in x -- so the FOOTING is a minor axis here and the CONVENTION is the major one.
  [OK] the verdict is robust across the whole 2.6-dex convention fork -- the SOFTEST convention anywhere (corpus single-absorber (S1, z=2.8)) still gives 3 sigma on the calibration channel -- but the SIZE of the number is convention-owned to a factor 9, so no precise sigma should be quoted without naming the convention
  [OK] Aguirre's own identity reproduced: a_N/a0 = 1/30000 on their a0, and sqrt of that = 173.2 = their quoted a0/170 -- confirming the a0/170 figure is the MODIFIED acceleration, not the Newtonian ratio
  a0 PROPAGATED SELF-CONSISTENTLY through their Eqs. 7-8 (a_N ~ a0^(-1/5), L_J ~ a0^(-2/5)),
  since their a_N is backed out of the MOND relation and therefore inherits an a0 dependence:
